# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_lang_recall.py" "LANG RECALL GATE: PASS" "supported-language coupling recall (go embed + ruby mixin)" "supported-language coupling recall: a SUPPORTED language can carry a real cross-file dependency through a construct that emits NO calls edge, so the coupling is SILENTLY MISSED (recall hole = the worst failure, a missed collision read as clear). MEASURED two such holes in INSTALLED grammars and locked the fix: (1) GO STRUCT EMBEDDING -- type Derived struct { Base } embeds Base (Go's reuse/inheritance mechanism, methods PROMOTED never called); a SAME-PACKAGE embed has NO import AND NO call edge -> invisible (baseline emitted zero edges while the sibling composite-literal Base{} correctly emitted calls->Base, the exact #253-class hole that Go wires via composition not calls); fix emits the embedded type NAME as a content-free calls edge, guarded by the no-field-identifier rule so a NAMED field's type ANNOTATION (the measured-noisy case the spec excludes) never couples. (2) RUBY MIXIN -- include/extend/prepend M (the Rails concern idiom, the Ruby analogue of implements) parses as a call whose callee is the UBIQUITOUS hub include and whose ARGUMENT is the module constant, so the generic path emitted calls->include and DROPPED the module name (measured on an autoload-style repo with NO require: the Dog<->Walkable dependency was completely invisible); fix emits calls->M (the module constant) instead of the hub callee, the SAME special-casing require/require_relative already get. Both dsts are BARE NAMES (content-free) that flow through the EXACT _claim_adjacency resolution every call passes -- defs<=3 fan-out cap, import-confirmation, single-definer, hub dampening -- so a multi-definer/external target is DROPPED not fanned out (the gate never resolves itself). PROVEN: go-embed recall + precision (named-field annotation stays clear) + control (named-field-only struct emits no edge), ruby-mixin recall + namespaced + precision (the include hub never couples) + control (an ordinary receiver call still emits its calls edge, no regression). CI-DETERMINISTIC: each language is checked ONLY if its grammar is installed (probed via _ts_languages); an absent grammar is SKIPPED (skip-pass) -- environment, never a bug" "supported-language coupling recall: Go struct embedding and Ruby mixins are real cross-file dependencies the call graph cannot see -- now captured as content-free bare-name calls edges through the existing resolver; recall-safe and precision-preserving (named-field annotations stay clear, the include/extend hub never couples, ordinary calls unaffected), and skip-pass for any uninstalled grammar" 24
